From 32ce5ef62a376205eb0ce05cc50808644e55b9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:09:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sparc64: advance PROM console output by the bytes written

A short firmware write advances buf by the remaining length rather
than the number of bytes consumed. This can resend the wrong bytes or
read beyond the caller's buffer. Advance by the returned count instead.

The old loop retried negative returns indefinitely. Stop on errors,
zero progress or an impossible count, dropping the remaining text
instead of spinning indefinitely or walking beyond the buffer. This
can lose output on a transient error; it deliberately bounds software
retrying, not the duration of a firmware call itself.

Fixes: 595a251c0740 ("sparc: Write to prom console using indirect buffer.")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
index 86dace787ae6..f3566e8f7083 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/prom/console_64.c
@@ -38,9 +38,9 @@ void prom_console_write_buf(const char *buf, int len)
 {
 	while (len) {
 		int n = __prom_console_write_buf(buf, len);
-		if (n < 0)
-			continue;
+		if (n <= 0 || n > len)
+			break;
 		len -= n;
-		buf += len;
+		buf += n;
 	}
 }
